      ],
      "nets": [
        "GND",
        "Net-(D2-K)"
      ],
      "observed": "C2 is a 100 nF capacitor connected between the servo power rail Net-(D2-K) and GND, while C1/C3/C4 are 100 uF capacitors on the same rail.",
      "expected": "The specification states that C1–C4 are 100 µF × 4 bulk capacitors on the servo power rail downstream of D2; C2 should therefore be 100 µF.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C2\")\n      (value \"100n\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C2\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C2\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C1–C4 | 100 µF × 4 | Bulk capacitance on the servo power rail (downstream of D2), buffering the high inrush current of PWM servos."
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C2 0 Net-_D2-K_ 100n"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The servo rail has 1000× less capacitance at C2 than intended, reducing bulk energy storage and inrush-current buffering; PWM servos are more likely to cause voltage sag or M5Stack brownout.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The connectivity and most component values match the specification, but C2 is a 100 nF capacitor in the servo bulk-capacitor bank where the spec requires 100 µF, which is a clear value deviation."
}

